ot automatically the fundamental."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:c":{"hint":"Mark the boundary conditions at both ends, then fit the simplest allowed pattern between them.","notes":["Fixed string ends and closed pipe ends are displacement nodes; an open pipe end is a displacement antinode. Adjacent nodes are λ/2 apart; a node and adjacent antinode are λ/4 apart.","Two like ends allow L = nλ/2. One open and one closed end allows L = (2n − 1)λ/4. Use the mode shown, not automatically the fundamental.","Link the relevant physical cause to the observation asked about. Naming a law alone does not explain why this particular result follows."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:d":{"hint":"Locate the nodes separating the two points before comparing their oscillations.","notes":["Points within one loop of a standing wave oscillate in phase; adjacent loops oscillate in antiphase. Amplitude depends on position.","An ideal standing wave forms from opposite-travelling waves of equal frequency and has no net energy transport along the pattern. The nodes remain at zero displacement."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:e":{"hint":"Mark the boundary conditions at both ends, then fit the simplest allowed pattern between them.","notes":["Fixed string ends and closed pipe ends are displacement nodes; an open pipe end is a displacement antinode. Adjacent nodes are λ/2 apart; a node and adjacent antinode are λ/4 apart.","Two like ends allow L = nλ/2. One open and one closed end allows L = (2n − 1)λ/4. Use the mode shown, not automatically the fundamental."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:f.i":{"hint":"Mark the boundary conditions at both ends, then fit the simplest allowed pattern between them.","notes":["Fixed string ends and closed pipe ends are displacement nodes; an open pipe end is a displacement antinode. Adjacent nodes are λ/2 apart; a node and adjacent antinode are λ/4 apart.","Two like ends allow L = nλ/2. One open and one closed end allows L = (2n − 1)λ/4. Use the mode shown, not automatically the fundamental."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:f.ii":{"hint":"Mark the boundary conditions at both ends, then fit the simplest allowed pattern between them.","notes":["Fixed string ends and closed pipe ends are displacement nodes; an open pipe end is a displacement antinode. Adjacent nodes are λ/2 apart; a node and adjacent antinode are λ/4 apart.","Two like ends allow L = nλ/2. One open and one closed end allows L = (2n − 1)λ/4. Use the mode shown, not automatically the fundamental."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:f.iii":{"hint":"Mark the boundary conditions at both ends, then fit the simplest allowed pattern between them.","notes":["Fixed string ends and closed pipe ends are displacement nodes; an open pipe end is a displacement antinode. Adjacent nodes are λ/2 apart; a node and adjacent antinode are λ/4 apart.","Two like ends allow L = nλ/2. One open and one closed end allows L = (2n − 1)λ/4. Use the mode shown, not automatically the fundamental."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:g.i":{"hint":"Mark the boundary conditions at both ends, then fit the simplest allowed pattern between them.","notes":["Fixed string ends and closed pipe ends are displacement nodes; an open pipe end is a displacement antinode. Adjacent nodes are λ/2 apart; a node and adjacent antinode are λ/4 apart.","Two like ends allow L = nλ/2. One open and one closed end allows L = (2n − 1)λ/4. Use the mode shown, not automatically the fundamental."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:g.ii":{"hint":"Mark the boundary conditions at both ends, then fit the simplest allowed pattern between them.","notes":["Fixed string ends and closed pipe ends are displacement nodes; an open pipe end is a displacement antinode. Adjacent nodes are λ/2 apart; a node and adjacent antinode are λ/4 apart.","Two like ends allow L = nλ/2. One open and one closed end allows L = (2n − 1)λ/4. Use the mode shown, not automatically the fundamental."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:h":{"hint":"Mark the boundary conditions at both ends, then fit the simplest allowed pattern between them.","notes":["Fixed string ends and closed pipe ends are displacement nodes; an open pipe end is a displacement antinode. Adjacent nodes are λ/2 apart; a node and adjacent antinode are λ/4 apart.","Two like ends allow L = nλ/2. One open and one closed end allows L = (2n − 1)λ/4. Use the mode shown, not automatically the fundamental."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:i":{"hint":"Mark the boundary conditions at both ends, then fit the simplest allowed pattern between them.","notes":["Fixed string ends and closed pipe ends are displacement nodes; an open pipe end is a displacement antinode. Adjacent nodes are λ/2 apart; a node and adjacent antinode are λ/4 apart.","Two like ends allow L = nλ/2. One open and one closed end allows L = (2n − 1)λ/4. Use the mode shown, not automatically the fundamental."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:j":{"hint":"Mark the boundary conditions at both ends, then fit the simplest allowed pattern between them.","notes":["Fixed string ends and closed pipe ends are displacement nodes; an open pipe end is a displacement antinode. Adjacent nodes are λ/2 apart; a node and adjacent antinode are λ/4 apart.","Two like ends allow L = nλ/2. One open and one closed end allows L = (2n − 1)λ/4. Use the mode shown, not automatically the fundamental."]},"sup-568e3677282fa095-w1:k":{"hint":"Compare the driving frequency with the system’s natural frequency, then consider the damping.","notes":["Resonance is a large forced response when the driving frequency is near a natural frequency. Energy must be supplied by the driver.","More damping reduces the peak response and broadens the resonance. Distinguish driving frequency from the free oscillation that would occur without the driver."]}}},"answers":{"entries":{}},"presentation":{"practice/supplement/sup-568e3677282fa095-1-answer-e-a4b078b7af2adf12.webp":{"crop":[0,0,1124,164],"size":[1124,200]},"practice/supplement/sup-568e3677282fa095-1-g.ii-ff4c94946b3a1547.webp":{"crop":[0,0,1124,39],"size":[1124